INT. FARMHOUSE KITCHEN - MORNING

Pancakes burn. Smoke curls from the pan.

MAMA ROSALIE, 40s, dishtowel on her shoulder, flips the pan. Too late. Black.

                    MAMA ROSALIE
Boys! Breakfast!

Thundering feet. TUCKER, 10, and BEN, 8, skid in, socks sliding.

                    TUCKER
It's on fire!

                    BEN
It's not on fire. It's crispy.

                    MAMA ROSALIE
Sit.

They sit. Tucker pokes a pancake with a fork. It crunches.

A KNOCK at the screen door. Everyone stops.

A MAN in a rumpled suit stands on the porch, hat in hand, a battered suitcase at his feet. Forty-ish, kind eyes, sunburned nose.

                    MAN
Morning, folks.

Mama Rosalie's face goes slack.

                    MAMA ROSALIE
Amos?

                    TUCKER
Who's that?

The man steps inside. Sets down the suitcase.

                    AMOS
Hello, Tuck.

Tucker slides off his chair. Edges behind his mother.

                    BEN
Is that Daddy?

Amos kneels, arms open. Ben looks at his mother. She nods, barely. He runs.
